  "goodToKnow": "Der Weltrekord is a world record: einen Weltrekord aufstellen (set), brechen (break), halten. East German athlete Marita Koch's 400 m world record of 47.60 seconds from 1985 still stands, though many GDR records are overshadowed by the state doping programme. Der Rekord is pronounced re-KORT. Rekordverdächtig means potentially record-breaking. Plural: die Weltrekorde."
